Research Gaps and Unresolved Issues

The papers identify several research gaps:

AI-generated code may contain security vulnerabilities.
LLMs sometimes generate incorrect or insecure code.
Cloud-native security solutions need better automation.
Vulnerability detection tools still struggle with accuracy.
There is limited integration between AI-assisted coding and automated security testing.
More real-world evaluations are required before AI can be fully trusted in software engineering.
Contribution to the Research Topic

Each paper contributes differently to understanding AI and software security.

Hou et al. (2024) explains how AI is changing software development through Large Language Models.
Psomas et al. (2023) provides foundational knowledge of cloud-native security and modern software deployment.
Lin et al. (2024) focuses on protecting software by improving vulnerability detection using machine learning.

Together, these papers provide a comprehensive understanding of modern software engineering by combining AI innovation, cloud security, and software vulnerability management. They demonstrate that while AI significantly improves software development efficiency, security remains a critical challenge requiring further research.

Conclusion

The selected papers provide a balanced literature review by covering recent advancements, foundational concepts, and ongoing challenges in software engineering. Artificial Intelligence, cloud-native technologies, and automated vulnerability detection are shaping the future of software development. However, improving AI reliability, strengthening cloud security, and reducing software vulnerabilities remain important research priorities.
